  "question": {
    "text": "Let the tangent to the circle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn></math>&nbsp;at the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo></math> meet <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> -axis and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi></math>-axis at point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math>, respectively. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math> is the radius of the circle passing through the origin <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi></math> and having centre at the incentre of the triangle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> is equal to"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>529</mn><mn>64</mn></mfrac></math>",
